# Business Problem

## Background

Klik2learn is an online learning platform that supports learners with English and digital learning activities.

As part of my internship, I analysed learner data to understand student engagement, activity and academic performance.

The analysis looked at how students were using the learning platform and how their engagement related to their progress.

## Business Problem

The available learner data contained useful information about student activity and performance, but it was not always easy to identify:

- which students were actively engaging with the platform;
- how engagement changed over time;
- which students were making progress;
- which students showed limited or no improvement; and
- where additional support or intervention might be useful.

This created an opportunity to use the data to identify patterns in learner behaviour and improve how student progress and engagement are communicated through the dashboard.

## Project Objective

The objective of the analysis was to understand student engagement and performance and use the findings to recommend improvements to the student dashboard.

The analysis focused on:

- learner activity;
- weekly engagement;
- time spent learning;
- academic progress;
- changes in performance; and
- identifying students who may need additional support.

## Key Question

How can learner engagement and performance data be analysed and presented more effectively to help Klik2learn understand student progress and identify where additional support may be needed?

## Expected Outcome

The analysis was intended to provide:

- clear insights into learner engagement and performance;
- identification of important patterns and areas of concern;
- evidence-based recommendations; and
- suggestions for improving the student dashboard.
